\title{metrictrails: Processing of GNSS Streams from Sports Watches}
\description{
Tools to read, clean and standardise GNSS streams recorded by sports
watches and similar devices, with a focus on trail and mountain running.

A \emph{stream} is a sequence of consecutive readings with \code{lon} and \code{lat} and,
optionally, \code{ele}, \code{timestamp}, \code{time} and other variables (heart rate,
cadence, ...). The recommended pipeline is:
\enumerate{
\item \code{\link[=read_stream]{read_stream()}}: read a GPX file.
\item \code{\link[=uniform_stream]{uniform_stream()}}: apply the naming convention.
\item \code{\link[=sanitize_stream]{sanitize_stream()}}: smooth the coordinates and flag implausible
readings.
\item \code{\link[=resample_stream]{resample_stream()}}: resample to a uniform spatial resolution derived
from the Nyquist criterion (\code{\link[=resolution_stream]{resolution_stream()}}).
\item \code{\link[=ele_correction]{ele_correction()}}: replace elevation with values from a Digital
Elevation Model (\code{\link[=get_dem]{get_dem()}}, \code{\link[=resample_dem]{resample_dem()}}).
}

Once the stream is tidy:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=differential_stream]{differential_stream()}}, \code{\link[=summarise_stream]{summarise_stream()}}, \code{\link[=fractal_stream]{fractal_stream()}} and
\code{\link[=tobler_stream]{tobler_stream()}} compute derived measures;
\item \code{\link[=project_stream]{project_stream()}} adds UTM coordinates and \code{\link[=locate_stream]{locate_stream()}} projects
readings on a reference (linear referencing);
\item \code{\link[=compare_stream]{compare_stream()}} and \code{\link[=detect_stream]{detect_stream()}} compare a stream with another
stream or route;
\item \code{\link[=match_stream]{match_stream()}} aligns a stream along a reference trail it is known to
follow;
\item \code{\link[=write_stream]{write_stream()}} writes the result to GPX.
}
